#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# reverse_sort

#% text
# `reverse_sort(xs)` gives the elements of `xs` in reverse canonical order: numbers from the largest down.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is `reverse(sort(xs))`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
reverse_sort([3, 1, 2])
#% output
#= [3, 2, 1]

#% cell
reverse_sort(["b", "c", "a"])
#% output
#= ["c", "b", "a"]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The reverse of `sort`:

#% cell
reverse_sort([2, 5, 1]) == reverse(sort([2, 5, 1]))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sort`, `reverse`, `take_largest`
